# Package 3 — Temporal Consistency Aggregation (TCA)

## 1. Overview

This package implements Temporal Consistency Aggregation (TCA) for the Rip Current Detection project.

TCA processes frame-level soft segmentation masks to improve temporal consistency, maintain instance identities, and reduce short-lived detections.

The implementation is designed to integrate with Package 2's soft-mask cache and Package 4's T2 parameter-tuning pipeline.

## 2. Features

- Multi-instance tracking using Hungarian assignment and IoU matching
- Per-track temporal heatmap aggregation using an exponential moving average (EMA)
- Time-based presence, absence, and track timeout handling
- Gaussian smoothing and hysteresis thresholding
- Support for timestamps in seconds
- Per-video state reset
- COCO-like uncompressed RLE output for annotated frames
- Synthetic unit tests and performance profiling

